    "notes": "1. Revenue, Net Income (Group share), Taxes, and Interest Expenses are directly mapped from the primary statement. 2. Total Operating Cost is constructed by summing all operating expenses that reduce income: Cost of sales, Marketing and selling expenses, General and administrative expenses, and Other operating income and expenses (which is a net expense). The sign convention is followed: all values are positive as they reduce income. 3. 'Other financial income and expenses' is not included in interest_expenses as it contains non-interest items like dividends, FX, and fair value adjustments. 4. 'Income/(Loss) from joint ventures and associates' is not included in total_operating_cost as it is non-operating income. 5. The scale is 1,000,000 (EUR millions) as stated in the statement. 6. All numbers are extracted without parentheses; parentheses in the source indicate negative values, but per the sign convention rule (#10), expense items are reported as positive numbers.",
